Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — scene draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: SC015 proposed for individual author scene review; combined pass provisionally accepted

INT. HELEN AND BRIAN'S HOUSE - FRIDAY EVENING - ZOE'S ACCOUNT

Helen opens before Zoe can knock twice. She pulls Zoe inside and holds her until Zoe's knees nearly give. BRIAN looks past them to the street.

BRIAN
Did anyone see you? Follow you?

He locks and chains the door, checks it again, then turns off the porch light. The photographs, old shoes and Zoe's ceramic hedgehog are where she left them. The familiar room feels watched.

Helen asks if Zoe is hurt and offers to call police and a doctor. Brian asks what they will say about Zoe's papers and calls MAC first. Zoe refuses to surrender her backpack. Helen stops reaching for it. Later she cleans a scrape on Zoe's wrist and makes toast; Zoe can eat half a slice. Brian returns with Mac's order: no school, messages, Jackie, police or outside contact before he arrives.

Zoe locks her bedroom door, hides the folder and drive in her bag beneath the bed, and leaves them unread. At night voices rise through the heating vent.

BRIAN (O.S.)
The money won't matter if this comes out. What will we say about no proper adoption? Who arranged it?

HELEN (O.S.)
We raised her.

Zoe studies the childhood photographs, now unable to read them as reassurance.

INT. HELEN AND BRIAN'S LIVING ROOM/KITCHEN - SATURDAY - ZOE'S ACCOUNT

Mac arrives before nine. Helen and Brian quieten as he asks Zoe about the escape, the buses and anyone she contacted. She keeps the folder to herself. He orders no police, social services or hospital except through him. Helen protests that Zoe needs care. He calls the restriction protection.

MAC
She'll go to my mother. Her grandmother.

ZOE
Helen told me I didn't have one. Why do they listen to you?

Mac silences Brian with a raised finger. He will not answer beyond saying he knows what happens next. Before leaving he forbids Zoe to contact Jackie.

Afterward Helen reaches toward Zoe. Zoe steps back, seeing that her hurt is real.

ZOE
Why didn't you call the police when I disappeared? How did you search for me?

Helen cannot describe it. Brian says they did what they could without making matters worse. Zoe holds her backpack between them.

INT. ELIAS'S CAR - MOTORWAY - PRESENT DAY

ZOE
I think they loved me. That's why I can't throw it all away. I don't know which parts were real.

ELIAS
You may never get one clean answer. That doesn't mean you imagined the good parts. It doesn't erase what they failed to do.

Zoe remembers Jackie telling an old story: a watcher sent between rival crews, the only one to walk away when both attacked. She says the date. Elias eases the car into another lane and checks the mirror twice.

ELIAS
Interesting story.

ZOE
You've heard it before.

He does not answer. Zoe sees enough to register a connection, not its explanation.
